<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil cuts posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil cuts posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it lowered the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$3.00/cubic metre or C$0.47/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$164.00/cubic metre, or C$26.07/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$152.00/cubic metre, or C$24.17/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$124.00/cubic metre, or C$19.71/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$135.00/cubic metre, or C$21.46/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
